<% content_for :title, "Carline, Data-Driven — #{Profile.current.name}" %>

<p class="text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-600 tracking-wide uppercase mb-2">If the carline were a data problem</p>
<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Carline: pain, data, and eventually, joy</h1>
<p class="text-slate-600 max-w-2xl mb-2">
  Every school has one queue nobody's ever pointed a real database at. So I did.
</p>
<p class="text-xs text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mb-8">
  Not pulled from real data, but imagined from real carline woes :-) What's real is how I'd actually
  work it: not just the surface numbers, but digging, combining datasets, looking for patterns that
  weren't obvious on the first pass.
</p>

<div class="sticky top-0 z-30 -mx-6 px-6 py-3 mb-12 bg-indigo-50/95 backdrop-blur border-b border-indigo-200 shadow-sm flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-2 sm:gap-4">
  <span class="text-sm text-slate-700">Escape into a world where getting to your kid is just the click of a button. Jump the cone, dodge the loose dog, beat the clock.</span>
  <%= link_to "Play →", carline_play_path, class: "shrink-0 self-start sm:self-auto bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-700 text-white font-semibold rounded-lg px-4 py-2 text-sm" %>
</div>

<section class="mb-4">
  <%= form_with url: carline_path, method: :get, local: true, class: "flex gap-2 max-w-md" do %>
    <%= text_field_tag :q, @q, placeholder: "Search the log — try \"slow\" or \"guard\"", class: "flex-1 border border-slate-300 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm" %>
    <%= submit_tag "Search", class: "bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-900 text-white text-sm font-medium rounded-lg px-4 py-2 cursor-pointer" %>
  <% end %>
  <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">
    Keyword + synonym search today, not real semantic search — that's the natural next step once this points at a real vector-capable store instead of a hand-typed table.
  </p>
</section>

<% if @q %>
  <section class="mb-12 bg-white border border-indigo-200 rounded-lg p-5">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">Results for "<%= @q %>"</p>
    <% if @search[:days].none? && @search[:complaints].none? %>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">Nothing matched. Try "slow," "suv," "guard," "bike," or "loop."</p>
    <% else %>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-700">
        <% @search[:days].each do |d| %>
          <li>📅 <%= d.observed_on.strftime("%b %-d") %> — <%= d.note %></li>
        <% end %>
        <% @search[:complaints].each do |c| %>
          <li>💬 <%= c.logged_on.strftime("%b %-d") %> — <%= c.category %> (<%= c.channel %>, <%= c.family_label %>)</li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    <% end %>
  </section>
<% end %>

<section class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-4">
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">What the raw data shows</h2>
  <%= link_to "Export the report ↓", carline_export_path(q: @q), class: "text-sm font-medium text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800" %>
</section>

<section class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-4">
  <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
    <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-indigo-600"><%= @avg_wait %></p>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-1">avg. wait, minutes</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
    <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-indigo-600"><%= @worst_day&.worst_wait_minutes %></p>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-1">worst single wait</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
    <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-indigo-600"><%= @complaint_count %></p>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-1">complaints logged</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
    <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-indigo-600"><%= @days.count %></p>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-1">dismissals observed</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mb-12">
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">Complaints by category</h2>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    <% @complaints_by_category.sort_by { |_, n| -n }.each do |category, count| %>
      <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-full px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-slate-700">
        <span class="font-semibold text-indigo-600"><%= count %></span> <%= category %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<p class="text-sm text-slate-600 max-w-2xl mb-12">
  Read on its own, this says: <strong>the carline is slow, so fix the carline.</strong> Redesign the
  loop, stagger the grades, add a lane. All reasonable. All aimed at the symptom.
</p>

<section class="mb-16 bg-indigo-50 border border-indigo-200 rounded-lg p-6">
  <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-600 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Then we combined it with another dataset</p>
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">Family transport preferences — not just complaints</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 mb-4 max-w-2xl">
    The complaint log only shows who's annoyed. It doesn't show <em>why</em>, or what they'd actually
    prefer instead. So the related dataset here isn't more carline data — it's family-level data on
    who's in extended day and who's already said they'd take a bus if one existed.
  </p>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4">
    <div>
      <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900"><%= @vocal_families.size %></p>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">repeat-complaint families</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-indigo-600"><%= @vocal_bus_ready_percent %>%</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">of them are also extended-day families who already want a bus</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900"><%= @bus_ready_families.count %></p>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">families total who'd take a bus today, out of <%= @total_families %></p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 max-w-2xl">
    That's the hidden pattern: the loudest complaints aren't randomly distributed — they cluster with
    families who were already halfway to a different answer. What looked like a carline-efficiency
    problem is at least partly an <strong>afternoon-transport</strong> problem wearing a carline
    costume.
  </p>
  <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl">
    Honest footnote: a real 95% confidence interval at a ±5% margin needs roughly 384 families
    surveyed. This toy has 20. Real rigor means knowing your sample size before you trust your
    percentages — this page is a sketch of the method, not a finished study.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mb-16">
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">So — not one fix, three</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-6 max-w-2xl">
    Different effort, different timelines, different kinds of payoff — and they're not mutually
    exclusive. A and B both help how the existing line moves; C changes what's arriving in the first
    place. Stack C with either, and it shrinks the line before A or B even have to work as hard.
  </p>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
    <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-400 font-semibold mb-1">Option A</p>
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Earlier, organized check-in</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-3">
        App-based (or a simple tag scan) check-in when a car enters the queue, so kids are staged in
        rounds and ready to hop in — instead of being paged after the car's already at the front.
      </p>
      <dl class="text-xs text-slate-500 space-y-1">
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-600">Effort:</dt> <dd class="inline">Low-medium — a check-in point + staging process</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-600">Timeline:</dt> <dd class="inline">Weeks</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-600">Payoff alone:</dt> <dd class="inline">Faster hop-in, same number of cars</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-400 font-semibold mb-1">Option B</p>
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Stagger dismissal by grade</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-3">Spread the surge instead of releasing every classroom at once.</p>
      <dl class="text-xs text-slate-500 space-y-1">
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-600">Effort:</dt> <dd class="inline">Medium — scheduling, staff buy-in</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-600">Timeline:</dt> <dd class="inline">Weeks</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-600">Payoff alone:</dt> <dd class="inline">Lower peak congestion, sustained</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-600">Stacked with A:</dt> <dd class="inline">Smaller, faster-moving rounds instead of one long one</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-indigo-50 border border-indigo-300 rounded-lg p-5">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-indigo-500 font-semibold mb-1">Option C</p>
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Afternoon bus route</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-3">
        Route extended-day families who already want it. Fewer cars, new driver jobs, a new revenue
        line for the school, fewer trips for those families — and target the most vocal families
        first, since that's the lowest-friction path to visible satisfaction gains.
      </p>
      <dl class="text-xs text-slate-500 space-y-1">
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-600">Effort:</dt> <dd class="inline">High — planning, staffing, a route</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-600">Timeline:</dt> <dd class="inline">A semester</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-600">Payoff alone:</dt> <dd class="inline"><%= @bus_ready_families.count %> fewer cars in line, structurally</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-600">Stacked with A/B:</dt> <dd class="inline">Compounds — smaller line <em>and</em> it moves faster</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl">
    The honest next version of this page: a live toggle to combine options and see (and export) the
    specific projected outcome for whichever combination you'd actually pick. Not built yet — this
    pass sketches the tradeoffs, doesn't simulate them.
  </p>
</section>

<details class="mb-16 group">
  <summary class="cursor-pointer text-sm font-semibold text-slate-500 hover:text-indigo-600 select-none">
    Dismissal log (the raw artifact, if you want to poke at it) ▸
  </summary>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto mt-4">
    <table class="min-w-full text-sm border border-slate-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
      <thead class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-600 text-left">
        <tr>
          <th class="px-4 py-2">Date</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-2">Dismissal</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-2">Avg wait</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-2">Worst wait</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-2">Cars</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-2">Field notes</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 bg-white">
        <% @days.each do |day| %>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><%= day.observed_on.strftime("%b %-d") %></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2"><%= day.dismissal_time %></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2"><%= day.avg_wait_minutes %> min</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium text-indigo-600"><%= day.worst_wait_minutes %> min</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2"><%= day.cars_in_line %></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 text-slate-500"><%= day.note %></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</details>
